# Question 2: Student Marks Management System

**Problem Statement:**

A teacher wants to create a Java program to store the marks of students in a class. The number of students is not known in advance, so the program should use a dynamic array. The teacher can add marks one by one, and the array should automatically increase its size when it becomes full.

**Sample Input:**

```text
5
85
90
78
92
88
```

**Sample Output:**

```text
Marks of Students:
85 90 78 92 88

Total Marks: 433
Average Marks: 86.60
Highest Marks: 92
Lowest Marks: 78
```

**Java Code:**

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    private int[] marks;
    private int size;

    public Main() {
        marks = new int[2];
        size = 0;
    }

    // Add marks and increase array size when full
    public void addMarks(int mark) {
        if (size == marks.length) {
            int[] newMarks = new int[marks.length * 2];

            for (int i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {
                newMarks[i] = marks[i];
            }

            marks = newMarks;
        }

        marks[size] = mark;
        size++;
    }

    public void displayMarks() {
        int total = 0;
        int highest = marks[0];
        int lowest = marks[0];

        System.out.println("Marks of Students:");

        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            System.out.print(marks[i] + " ");
            total += marks[i];

            if (marks[i] > highest) {
                highest = marks[i];
            }

            if (marks[i] < lowest) {
                lowest = marks[i];
            }
        }

        double average = (double) total / size;

        System.out.println("\n");
        System.out.println("Total Marks: " + total);
        System.out.printf("Average Marks: %.2f%n", average);
        System.out.println("Highest Marks: " + highest);
        System.out.println("Lowest Marks: " + lowest);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        Main student = new Main();

        int n = sc.nextInt();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int mark = sc.nextInt();
            student.addMarks(mark);
        }

        student.displayMarks();

        sc.close();
    }
}
```

**Concept Used:**

* **Dynamic Array:** Starts with a fixed capacity and grows when full.
* **Array Resizing:** Creates a new array with double the previous capacity and copies existing marks.
* **Statistics:** Calculates total, average, highest, and lowest marks.
